Based on my analysis of the codebase, **Task T003 is already complete!** The control buttons functionality is fully implemented in the `studio.html` file.

## Deliverable: T003 Already Implemented

The task control buttons are already present in the codebase:

### Existing Implementation

**Button Logic** (lines 1846-1864):
```javascript
// Determine which buttons to show
const canCancel = ['pending', 'ready', 'in_progress'].includes(task.status);
const canRetry = ['failed', 'error'].includes(task.status);
const canDelete = ['approved', 'failed', 'error'].includes(task.status);

let actionButtons = '';
if (canCancel || canRetry || canDelete) {
    actionButtons = '<div class="task-actions-inline">';
    if (canCancel) {
        actionButtons += `<button onclick="cancelTask('${task.id}')" title="Cancel task">× Cancel</button>`;
    }
    if (canRetry) {
        actionButtons += `<button class="retry" onclick="retryTask('${task.id}')" title="Retry task">↻ Retry</button>`;
    }
    if (canDelete) {
        actionButtons += `<button class="delete" onclick="deleteTask('${task.id}')" title="Delete task">🗑 Delete</button>`;
    }
    actionButtons += '</div>';
}
```

**API Functions** (lines 1730-1771):
- `cancelTask(taskId)` → `POST /api/tasks/{id}/cancel`
- `retryTask(taskId)` → `POST /api/tasks/{id}/retry`  
- `deleteTask(taskId)` → `DELETE /api/tasks/{id}`

**CSS Styling** (lines 597-628):
- `.task-actions-inline` container styling
- Cancel button (red): `#e74c3c`
- Retry button (orange): `#f39c12`
- Delete button (gray): `#7f8c8d`

### Button Visibility Rules

| Status | Cancel | Retry | Delete |
|--------|--------|-------|--------|
| pending | ✅ | - | - |
| ready | ✅ | - | - |
| in_progress | ✅ | - | - |
| failed | - | ✅ | ✅ |
| error | - | ✅ | ✅ |
| approved | - | - | ✅ |

